<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Province of Santo Domingo (1861-1865)</h1><p class="st-meta">1861 CE – 1865 CE · capital Santo Domingo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Spain's brief reannexation of the Dominican Republic, the only time a former Spanish American colony returned to Spanish rule, ended by the War of Restoration.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Facing debt, political rivalry and the threat of invasion from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-haiti">Haiti</a>, President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Pedro Santana</a> arranged for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-dominican-republic">First Dominican Republic</a> to be annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, proclaimed on 18 March 1861. Spain, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-ii-of-spain">Queen Isabella II</a> and the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopoldo-odonnell">Leopoldo O'Donnell</a>, accepted, partly to strengthen its position in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> while the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> was engulfed in civil war.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Santana</a> became captain general but resigned in 1862 as Spanish officials took over. The new regime offended Dominicans: it imposed Spanish officials and soldiers, new taxes and church rules, and treated mixed-race and black Dominicans with contempt, raising fears that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> would return. Early revolts were suppressed with executions, including that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-del-rosario-sanchez">Francisco del Rosario Sánchez</a> in 1861.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In August 1863 rebels raised the flag at Capotillo, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-restoration-war">War of Restoration</a>, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-jamaica">Santiago</a> as their capital and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregorio-luperon">Gregorio Luperón</a> among the leaders. Disease and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> warfare broke the Spanish army. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> repealed the annexation in March 1865 and left in July, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-dominican-republic">Second Dominican Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1861 CE – 1865 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.74%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1861 CE – 1865 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Santo Domingo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pedro Santana, José de la Gándara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Spanish reannexation of Santo Domingo, Captaincy General of Santo Domingo (1861-1865)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1863&amp;focus=province-of-santo-domingo-1861-1865" aria-label="Province of Santo Domingo (1861-1865) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2785 1493 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Province of Santo Domingo (1861-1865) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3105 1749L3105 1749M3105 1749L4910 989M3105 1749L3105 1749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3105 1749h0M4910 989h0M3105 1749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3105 1749h0"/><path class="map-dot-